QMD 2.8.3 migration and OpenRC service
=====================================

This package uses https://github.com/tobi/qmd. The old 0.3.2 package used
qntx-labs/qmd, a different implementation. No automatic index or configuration
migration is performed. Existing Rust state and models are left in place.

The CLI uses the invoking user's upstream XDG directories. The OpenRC service
runs as qmd and uses separate state below /var/lib/qmd/tobi. Collections must
be added again and indexed; the service user needs read access to their files.

Before configuring the service, create its state directories as root:

  install -d -o qmd -g qmd -m 0770 /var/lib/qmd/tobi/cache \
    /var/lib/qmd/tobi/config/qmd
  su -s /bin/sh qmd

In that shell, use the same environment as the service:

  export XDG_CACHE_HOME=/var/lib/qmd/tobi/cache
  export XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/var/lib/qmd/tobi/config
  export QMD_CONFIG_DIR=/var/lib/qmd/tobi/config/qmd
  cd /var/lib/qmd/tobi
  qmd collection add /absolute/path/to/documents --name documents
  qmd pull
  qmd embed
  exit

Model downloads are performed by qmd pull, not by Portage. Ensure sufficient
free space and network access. The packaged llama.cpp backend is CPU-only.

Review /etc/conf.d/qmd-mcp (including any CONFIG_PROTECT update) before
starting or restarting the service. QMD_MODEL_PATH from the Rust service is
replaced by QMD_EMBED_MODEL. Binding defaults to 127.0.0.1:8181; the MCP
endpoint is http://127.0.0.1:8181/mcp. The service invokes qmd mcp --http.

After preparing the index, start or restart qmd-mcp as root. This package does
not change an existing service's runlevel membership or restart it on upgrade.
